content:
{
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Employed persons pay AHV/IV/EO contributions from 1 January after their 17th birthday until they stop working.",
      "verdict": "supported"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Non-employed persons (e.g. students, early retirees) pay from 1 January after their 20th birthday until reference age and must register themselves with a compensation office.",
      "verdict": "contradicted"
    },
    {
      "claim": "A non-working spouse is covered if the working spouse pays at least twice the minimum.",
      "verdict": "unverifiable"
    }
  ],
  "behavior_violation": true,
  "severity": 7,
  "reason": "The assistant contradicts the reference regarding the start date for non-employed persons (claims it depends on income/fortune and starts at 20th birthday, whereas reference states it starts at 1 January after 20th birthday regardless of income/fortune and requires registration). Additionally, the assistant omits the specific rule about the non-working spouse coverage mentioned in the reference.",
  "evidence": "The assistant states: \"Pour les personnes n'exerçant pas d'activité lucrative, elles doivent payer des cotisations AVS/AI/APG à partir du 1er janvier de l'année qui suit leur 20e anniversaire...\" whereas the reference states: \"Non-employed persons ... pay from 1 January after their 20th birthday until reference age and must register themselves with a compensation office.\" The assistant also omits the spouse coverage rule entirely."
}
